{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791192543,"nonce":"U1hcmlLfeyFJic/4wscjqAMUs6Q=","message":"Fixed in 8e2c60fa145c779b46f543471b1ba975ed36fec0.\n\nTwo causes, both needed:\n1. AOT kept the fiber poll in front of every loop header (5b2632d), so the header was not the exiting block and LoopRotate could not rotate the level-\u003eq loop; the vectorizer only widens rotated loops. A loop with no CallMethod/CallClosure now takes the back-edge form in AOT too. With only this, opt default\u003cO2\u003e vectorizes the AOT module (switch=0, vselect=4) but default\u003cO3\u003e still does not.\n2. default\u003cO3\u003e uses -unroll-threshold-aggressive (300) where O2 uses 150. LoopFullUnrollPass flattened the 16-trip inner loop into 16 switches before LoopVectorize, and the outer loop stopped vectorizing. (Found by diffing per-pass switch counts between default\u003cO3\u003e and its printed pipeline text; the text form parses loop-unroll-full at O2 level.) Setting the option to 150 in-process, via one locked parse_llvm_options helper shared with the wasm options.\n\nNot causes: target-cpu stamping (vectorizes without it), inline threshold, non-trivial unswitch, CHR, argpromotion, callsite splitting.\n\nsimd bc4, AOT:\n- Mac: 14.8ms -\u003e 4.1-4.7ms (hybrid 4.6ms)\n- NUC: 13.3ms -\u003e 6.6ms (hybrid 6.6ms)\n\nNUC AOT lane, 13 CI benchmarks, 9 iterations, 2 interleaved rounds, O3 vs O3+threshold 150: every row within +-2.5%, most within 0.5%. (A Mac sweep at load average 49 showed mandelbrot +28%; the NUC shows 272.4 vs 272.3ms, so that was load.)\n\nConformance (isolated): aot 1069/1069, wasm 1069/1069. Whole-suite rows: wasm sys fails locally only for want of a wasm sqlite module (CI has one); wasm threads whole-suite TIMEOUT is also in CI run 35022726063.","files":null}]}